{"once":{"id":"a6d424a5-359f-4c4e-836a-e94b76bf759f","word":"once","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"as soon as","word":"assim que"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"as soon as","word":"logo após/depois"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"as soon as","word":"tão logo"}],"pos":"conj","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"Near-synonym: immediately","id":"56e0dd85-b5ba-4c7a-91e9-2290af951fbe"},{"text":"We'll get a move on once we find the damn car keys!","bold_text_offsets":[[20,24]],"type":"example","id":"09f1e22a-067a-4dd8-8ef3-e2b5fc0876c9"},{"text":"Once you have obtained the elven bow, return to the troll bridge and trade it for the sleeping potion.","bold_text_offsets":[[0,4]],"type":"example","id":"dba36f6d-94bc-41d5-bdef-80eadc5ea46a"},{"text":"Once he is married, he will be able to claim the inheritance.","bold_text_offsets":[[0,4]],"type":"example","id":"d9d77685-3d2a-4818-b373-5db5284998dc"},{"text":"Not only were Jupp Heynckes' team pacey in attack but they were relentless in their pursuit of the ball once they had lost it, and as the game wore on they merely increased their dominance as City wilted in the Allianz Arena.","ref":"2011 September 27, Alistair Magowan, “Bayern Munich 2 - 0 Man City”, in BBC Sport:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[104,108]],"id":"7f06d41b-768b-4b74-a119-cb6ac7947109"},{"text":"In his submission to the UN, [Christof] Heyns points to the experience of drones. Unmanned aerial vehicles were intended initially only for surveillance, and their use for offensive purposes was prohibited, yet once strategists realised their perceived advantages as a means of carrying out targeted killings, all objections were swept out of the way.","ref":"2013 June 7, Ed Pilkington, “‘Killer robots’ should be banned in advance, UN told”, in The Guardian Weekly, volume 188, number 26, page 6:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[211,215]],"id":"6b8fab6d-eb6f-4ebf-9d6c-78c1c21beb0d"}],"links":[["As soon as","as soon as#Conjunction"],["when","when"],["after","after"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"immediately"}],"categories":["English links with manual fragments","English terms with quotations","English terms with usage examples"],"glosses":["As soon as; when; after."],"id":"8744776d-02f2-4617-8be8-a55ad5d232fc"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"once upon a time":{"id":"7e8b4602-c257-4bbb-9726-2562e91216e7","word":"once upon a time","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"traditional beginning of children’s stories, especially fairy tales","word":"era uma vez"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"traditional beginning of children’s stories, especially fairy tales","word":"havia uma vez"}],"pos":"adv","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"Once upon a time, in a faraway land, there lived a beautiful princess.","bold_text_offsets":[[0,16]],"type":"example","id":"599f3fdf-4c3f-433e-b454-030b5ac74ee2"},{"text":"There was once upon a time a charcoal-burner who had a son, and he was also a charcoal-burner.","ref":"1886, Peter Christen Asbjø￵rnsen, translated by H.L. Brækstad, Folk and Fairy Tales, page 308:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[10,26]],"id":"d1af42ad-9a68-4ca9-bfcc-c77864061f2a"},{"text":"Once upon a time, there was a Goblin Queen\nAnd she lived in a grand palace...","ref":"2023, A. C. MacDonald, Twistwood Tales (comic), Andrews McMeel, →ISBN, page 138:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[0,16]],"id":"91f47c40-b735-480f-aac7-bb8e5db417dc"}],"links":[["stories","story#English"],["fairy tale","fairy tale#English"]],"categories":["English terms with quotations","English terms with usage examples"],"glosses":["A long time ago; at some time in the past (a traditional beginning of children's stories, especially fairy tales)."],"tags":["not-comparable"],"id":"25c0dd6a-f09b-49b2-a344-88c3915b21a1"},{"examples":[{"text":"Long before popular music evolved its many genres and subgenres, the industry was driven by a simple one-size-fits-all philosophy […] Songwriters, once upon a time, wrote songs for the masses.","ref":"2012, Christoper Zara, chapter 2, in Tortured Artists: From Picasso and Monroe to Warhol and Winehouse, the Twisted Secrets of the World's Most Creative Minds, page 51:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[147,163]],"id":"c2637ea5-6014-4c54-84b1-86a96410a00c"}],"links":[["Formerly","formerly"]],"categories":["English terms with quotations"],"glosses":["Formerly."],"tags":["not-comparable"],"id":"4920a464-4c16-420b-93ec-9a6dabccff7c"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[{"sense":"a long time ago","word":"anciently"},{"word":"way back"},{"word":"long ago"}]},"once and for all":{"id":"568f316f-1ab5-4c54-8933-37414ccaa827","word":"once and for all","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"conclusively, finally, permanently","word":"de uma vez por todas"}],"pos":"adv","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"They replaced the entire door, in hopes of correcting the sticking and squeaking once and for all.","bold_text_offsets":[[81,97]],"type":"example","id":"d1715e48-ad24-4c3b-8377-a3e8c88292a6"}],"categories":["English adverbs","English coordinated pairs","English entries with incorrect language header","English idioms","English lemmas","English multiword terms","English terms with usage examples","English uncomparable adverbs","Entries with translation boxes","Pages with 1 entry","Pages with entries","Terms with Albanian translations","Terms with Ancient Greek translations","Terms with Arabic translations","Terms with Armenian translations","Terms with Asturian translations","Terms with Bulgarian translations","Terms with Catalan translations","Terms with Czech translations","Terms with Dutch translations","Terms with Esperanto translations","Terms with Finnish translations","Terms with French translations","Terms with Friulian translations","Terms with Galician translations","Terms wi